{"abstract":"In real-world machine learning (ML) pipelines, datasets are continuously growing. Models must incorporate this new training data to improve generalization and adapt to potential distribution shifts. The cost of model retraining is proportional to how frequently the model is retrained and how much data it is trained on, which makes the naive approach of retraining from scratch each time impractical. We present Modyn, a data-centric end-to-end machine learning platform. Modyn's ML pipeline abstraction enables users to declaratively describe policies for continuously training a model on a growing dataset. Modyn pipelines allow users to apply data selection policies (to reduce the number of data points) and triggering policies (to reduce the number of trainings). Modyn executes and orchestrates these continuous ML training pipelines. The system is open-source and comes with an ecosystem of benchmark datasets, models, and tooling. We formally discuss how to measure the performance of ML pipelines by introducing the concept of composite models, enabling fair comparison of pipelines with different data selection and triggering policies. We empirically analyze how various data selection and triggering policies impact model accuracy, and also show that Modyn enables high throughput training with sample-level data selection.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Böther, Maximilian","Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","Gsteiger, Viktor","Holzinger, Robin","Ma, Xianzhe","Tözün, Pinar","Klimovic, Ana"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798527"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zürich","Technical University of Munich"],"keyword":["Data centric AI","Machine Learning Pipelines","Online learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modyn data centric machine learning pipeline orchestration","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3709705","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Ties Robroek is supported by the Independent Research Fund Denmark’s Sapere Aude program (grant agreement number 0171-00061B)."],"id":"S01-000.00-798527","ids":["itu-3c4867ca-0f54-4916-93c9-ee174f2843d9"],"keyword":["data-centric ai","machine learning pipelines","online learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-19092CC39DB1CB3CDBA0E1B8E3F5D95C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3709705","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.mboether.com/assets/pdf/bother2025modyn.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Resource-Aware Data Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maximilian","key":"bötherpau","last":"Böther","name":"Böther, Maximilian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Titus Theodorus (Ties)","key":"robroekpau","last":"Robroek","locid":"42c316a3-1a31-469b-b436-635edc389e02","name":"Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","orcid":"0009-0006-3451-5602","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Viktor","key":"gsteigerpau","last":"Gsteiger","name":"Gsteiger, Viktor","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"holzingerpau","last":"Holzinger","name":"Holzinger, Robin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianzhe","key":"mapau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Xianzhe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pınar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","name_org":"Tözün, Pınar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ana","key":"klimovicpau","last":"Klimovic","name":"Klimovic, Ana","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-3c4867ca-0f54-4916-93c9-ee174f2843d9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modyn: Data-Centric Machine Learning Pipeline Orchestration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798527","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Machine learning (ML) benchmarks are crucial for evaluating the performance, efficiency, and scalability of ML systems, especially as the adoption of complex ML pipelines, such as retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), continues to grow. These pipelines introduce intricate execution graphs that require more advanced benchmarking approaches. Additionally, collocating workloads can improve resource efficiency but may introduce contention challenges that must be carefully managed. Detailed insights into resource utilization are necessary for effective collocation and optimized edge deployments. However, existing benchmarking frameworks often fail to capture these critical aspects.We introduce a modular end-to-end ML benchmarking framework designed to address these gaps. Our framework emphasizes modularity and reusability by enabling reusable pipeline stages, facilitating flexible benchmarking across diverse ML workflows. It supports complex workloads and measures their end-to-end performance. The workloads can be collocated, with the framework providing insights into resource utilization and contention between the concurrent workloads.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bayer, Robert","Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","Tözün, Pinar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818243"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Benchmarking","Deep learning","Edge computing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards a modular end to end machine learning benchmarking framework","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3719159.3721223","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818243","identifier":[{"id":"105003119925","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7702f384-2591-4960-abce-f443e9eac67d"],"keyword":["Benchmarking","Deep Learning","Edge Computing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A776E7A4C0A5304F8C95A70568919C38"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3719159.3721223","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://robertbayer.github.io/publication/towards-modular-benchmark/towards-modular-benchmark.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Resource-Aware Data Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"bayerpau","last":"Bayer","locid":"71115e9d-836f-409e-8c75-27d2de3e9caa","name":"Bayer, Robert","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Titus Theodorus (Ties)","key":"robroekpau","last":"Robroek","locid":"42c316a3-1a31-469b-b436-635edc389e02","name":"Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","orcid":"0009-0006-3451-5602","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-7702f384-2591-4960-abce-f443e9eac67d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards A Modular End-To-End Machine Learning Benchmarking Framework","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818243","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Deep learning training is an expensive process that extensively uses GPUs. However, not all model training saturates modern powerful GPUs. To create guidelines for such cases, this paper examines the performance of the different collocation methods available on NVIDIA GPUs: naïvely submitting multiple processes on the same GPU using multiple streams, utilizing Multi-Process Service (MPS), and enabling the MultiInstance GPU (MIG). Our results demonstrate that collocating multiple model training runs yields significant benefits, leading to up to three times training throughput despite increased epoch time. On the other hand, the aggregate memory footprint and compute needs of the models trained in parallel must fit the available memory and compute resources of the GPU. MIG can be beneficial thanks to its interference-free partitioning but can suffer from sub-optimal GPU utilization with dynamic or mixed workloads. In general, we recommend MPS as the best-performing and most flexible form of collocation for a single user submitting training jobs.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","Yousefzadeh-Asl-Miandoab, Ehsan","Tözün, Pinar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747244"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Collocation methods","Compute resources","Deep learning training","GPU utilization","Memory footprint","Model training","Multi Instance GPU MIG","Multi Process Service MPS","NVIDIA GPUs","Training throughput"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an analysis of collocation on gpus for deep learning training","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu-dasyalab.github.io/RAD/publication/papers/collocation_analysisi_euromlsys2024.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747244","identifier":[{"id":"85192265987","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8b5e5d8e-ab9e-4d7b-90f5-806f4ae31520"],"keyword":["Collocation methods","Compute resources","Deep learning training","GPU utilization","Memory footprint","Model training","Multi-Instance GPU (MIG)","Multi-Process Service (MPS)","NVIDIA GPUs","Training throughput"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A1622DC3C16BF5AE7FC02BA344E120AD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu-dasyalab.github.io/RAD/publication/papers/collocation_analysisi_euromlsys2024.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Titus Theodorus (Ties)","key":"robroekpau","last":"Robroek","locid":"42c316a3-1a31-469b-b436-635edc389e02","name":"Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","orcid":"0009-0006-3451-5602","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ehsan","key":"yousefzadehaslmiandoabpau","last":"Yousefzadeh-Asl-Miandoab","locid":"ac400e55-5188-4efd-872a-12df089e7068","name":"Yousefzadeh-Asl-Miandoab, Ehsan","orcid":"0000-0003-0156-1435","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3642970.3655827","isbn":["9798400705410"],"pages":"81-90","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 4th Workshop on Machine Learning and Systems, EuroMLSys 2024, Athens, Greece, 22 April 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85192265987"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8b5e5d8e-ab9e-4d7b-90f5-806f4ae31520"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An Analysis of Collocation on GPUs for Deep Learning Training","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747244","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Data Science is a field that has seen rapid development as of late due to the introduction of more powerful and specialised hardware. Massive algorithms such as Deep Neural Networks can be feasibly run on current-day accelerators. This hardware is by design efficient for solving embarrassingly parallel tasks, such as matrix multiplication. New models are sometimes trained on systems spanning over 10000 nodes with these accelerators, pushing the state of the art further but incurring massive resource costs [1, 2, 3]. Firstly, larger hardware setups require significant space, data-centre cooling and electricity [4, 5]. Secondly, with the state-of-the art utilising more and more expensive hardware setups, doing groundbreaking research in Machine Learning is becoming more expensive, and by extension, less attainable. It is vital to keep research accessible to not just those with private budgets [4]. Previous research has shown that the price of server infrastructure does not linearly reduce the time to train a Deep Learning model to accuracy. In some cases, models can be trained to similar accuracy with only a slight increase in training time on cheaper hardware [6]. It is thus crucial that we do not simply look at maximum accuracy, but also look at how long it takes us to get there [7, 1]. Paramount to training models in a resource-conscious way is to understand how Deep Learning training interacts with the hardware. Therefore, we have introduced the data collection and visualisation framework radT to make this information accessible. This allows Deep Learning researchers to make more informed choices on how they use their hardware. Additionally, we have used radT ourselves to run extensive benchmarking of Deep Learning training on a plethora of configurations. Furthermore, current-day GPU hardware may be more powerful than what is required to train a singular model. Rather than letting the unused resources go to waste, one can train multiple models at the same time on the same GPU (collocation). With radT we investigated the effectiveness of several methods of GPU collocation. This showed that GPU collocation can be very effective when models are small, or when models complement each other’s hardware requirements. Another way to increase efficiency via collocation is to streamline data loading and processing pipelines. We introduced a system that takes care of data redundancies by decoupling data loading from model training. This way, a server runs a single data loading process that loads data for all models being trained at the same time. This results in significant CPU savings and can even lead to GPU savings in cases where parts of the data pre-processing pipeline run on the GPU. While the aforementioned projects improve the transparency of resource utilisation and efficiency via collocation, they do not improve the training performance of a model training in isolation. Our final contribution makes use of our data loading expertise to design a new data loader that progressively increases the complexity of the data. By starting with easier data points before progressing to more complex data points, akin to how a human would learn, we are reducing the flops required for similar training steps. This leads to sharper accuracy growth and overall improved training speeds. With all of these resource-aware techniques, this thesis demonstrates that it is possible to achieve more in model training by using fewer resources.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798528"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"resourceful learning training more models with fewer resources","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"do","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://en.itu.dk/-/media/EN/Research/PhD-Programme/PhD-defences/2024/PhD-thesis-Temporary-Version-TR-pdf.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798528","ids":["itu-47229b31-3a7c-4916-90ed-79bc6dd5638a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-ADD4ED9BB3AA029CF31DD276BA3351F8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Titus Theodorus (Ties)","key":"robroekpau","last":"Robroek","locid":"42c316a3-1a31-469b-b436-635edc389e02","name":"Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","orcid":"0009-0006-3451-5602","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["N/A"],"issn":["16023536"],"issue":"230","pages":"127","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","series":"ITU-DS","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-47229b31-3a7c-4916-90ed-79bc6dd5638a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Resourceful Learning: Training More Models with Fewer Resources","type":"Other","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798528","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Evaluating hardware for deep learning is challenging. The models can take days or more to run, the datasets are generally larger than what fits into memory, and the models are sensitive to interference. Scaling this up to a large amount of experiments and keeping track of both software and hardware metrics thus poses real difficulties as these problems are exacerbated by sheer experimental data volume. This paper explores some of the data management and exploration difficulties when working on machine learning systems research. We introduce our solution in the form of an open-source framework built on top of a machine learning lifecycle platform. Additionally, we introduce a web environment for visualizing and exploring experimental data.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","Duane, Aaron","Yousefzadeh-Asl-Miandoab, Ehsan","Tözün, Pinar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718908"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data management","Deep Learning Evaluation","Hardware Metrics","Large Datasets","Open Source Framework"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data management and visualization for benchmarking deep learning training systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu-dasyalab.github.io/RAD/publication/papers/DEEM2023.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718908","identifier":[{"id":"85168369486","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b59cb1ae-b83b-4fde-b9dc-6ef7eaccc9bb"],"keyword":["Data Management","Deep Learning Evaluation","Hardware Metrics","Large Datasets","Open-Source Framework"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F93CD88E9FC521C5D4AF86777243B50F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://itu-dasyalab.github.io/RAD/publication/papers/DEEM2023.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Titus Theodorus (Ties)","key":"robroekpau","last":"Robroek","locid":"42c316a3-1a31-469b-b436-635edc389e02","name":"Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","orcid":"0009-0006-3451-5602","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aaron","key":"duanepau","last":"Duane","name":"Duane, Aaron","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ehsan","key":"yousefzadehaslmiandoabpau","last":"Yousefzadeh-Asl-Miandoab","locid":"ac400e55-5188-4efd-872a-12df089e7068","name":"Yousefzadeh-Asl-Miandoab, Ehsan","orcid":"0000-0003-0156-1435","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3595360.3595851","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Seventh Workshop on Data Management for End-to-End Machine Learning, DEEM 2023, Seattle, WA, USA, 18 June 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168369486"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b59cb1ae-b83b-4fde-b9dc-6ef7eaccc9bb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Data Management and Visualization for Benchmarking Deep Learning Training Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718908","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The embarrassingly parallel nature of deep learning training tasks makes CPU-GPU co-processors the primary commodity hardware for them. The computing and memory requirements of these tasks, however, do not always align well with the available GPU resources. It is, therefore, important to monitor and profile the behavior of training tasks on co-processors to understand better the requirements of different use cases. In this paper, our goal is to shed more light on the variety of tools for profiling and monitoring deep learning training tasks on server-grade NVIDIA GPUs. In addition to surveying the main characteristics of the tools, we analyze the functional limitations and overheads of each tool by using a both light and heavy training scenario. Our results show that monitoring tools like nvidia-smi and dcgm can be integrated with resource managers for online decision making thanks to their low overheads. On the other hand, one has to be careful about the set of metrics to correctly reason about the GPU utilization. When it comes to profiling, each tool has its time to shine; a framework-based or system-wide GPU profiler can first detect the frequent kernels or bottlenecks, and then, a lower-level GPU profiler can focus on particular kernels at the micro-architectural-level.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Yousefzadeh-Asl-Miandoab, Ehsan","Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","Tözün, Pinar"],"cuid":["S02-086.96-813958"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CPU GPU co processors","Deep learning","Monitoring","NVIDIA GPUs","Optimization","Performance monitoring","Profiling","co processors"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"profiling and monitoring deep learning training tasks","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3578356.3592589","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.96-813958","ids":["itu-1bfc6ba0-f044-4ad1-9511-27c1e9925dcf","itu-bfb83b46-73f5-494f-a042-a5f9b0e96c82"],"keyword":["CPU-GPU Co-processors","NVIDIA GPUs","Performance Monitoring","Training Task Profiling","co-processors","deep learning","monitoring","optimization","profiling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FD8D757C631605EF0BD5B0922486FB23"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3578356.3592589","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ehsan","key":"yousefzadehaslmiandoabpau","last":"Yousefzadeh-Asl-Miandoab","locid":"ac400e55-5188-4efd-872a-12df089e7068","name":"Yousefzadeh-Asl-Miandoab, Ehsan","orcid":"0000-0003-0156-1435","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Titus Theodorus (Ties)","key":"robroekpau","last":"Robroek","locid":"42c316a3-1a31-469b-b436-635edc389e02","name":"Robroek, Titus Theodorus (Ties)","orcid":"0009-0006-3451-5602","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pinar","key":"tözünpau","last":"Tözün","locid":"63342b24-28ec-40c5-a7d9-ec49867dc75d","name":"Tözün, Pinar","orcid":"0000-0001-6838-4854","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3578356.3592589","eisbn":["9798400700842"],"pages":"18-25","place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 3rd Workshop on Machine Learning and Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1bfc6ba0-f044-4ad1-9511-27c1e9925dcf","itu-bfb83b46-73f5-494f-a042-a5f9b0e96c82"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Profiling and Monitoring Deep Learning Training Tasks","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.96-813958","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
